{"repositoryId":1319440345,"availability":"available","full":"crmapache/smooth-stream-text","name":"smooth-stream-text","description":"Smooth out bursty LLM text streams and reveal them as a left-to-right wave. Zero dependencies, headless first, with React, Vue, Svelte and Web Component wrappers.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-01T16:19:06Z","updated":"2026-10-16T02:10:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://smooth-stream-text.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://smooth-stream-text.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.161Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.161Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.161Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.161Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["When a language model answers, the chunks arrive unevenly: one word, then twenty at once, then a pause while the server thinks. Rendering each chunk the moment it lands means the text stutters, and the eye reads the stutter before it reads the words.","smooth-stream-text buffers what arrives and releases it at a visually even rate, then reveals new text as a soft left-to-right wave.","model - the rate follows from holding a constant distance behind the live text, so it adapts to whatever is feeding it."],"features":["A real pacing controller. Not a fixed characters-per-second you tune per","Headless first. Take the smoothed string and render it however you already","Zero runtime dependencies. The core is pure logic and runs in Node, which is","Every framework. React, Vue, Svelte and a Web","Careful about the text itself. The text grows a character at a time, or a"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/crmapache/smooth-stream-text/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ee7c7431bf9af0d2a86cc5d4649a0c36cf3d073fd688ee1fa9d9544b4a2d11d6","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.248Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-